## SDD Specifications for "Establish Go Backend Architecture"

I've decomposed the idealization requirements into **15 focused, executable SDD specs** across 5 phases:

### **PHASE 1: Domain Foundation** (SDD-001 to SDD-005)

**SDD-001-NEW: Define domain types for Ingredient and Recipe**
```yaml
---
spec_id: SDD-001-NEW
title: Define domain types for Ingredient and Recipe
status: draft
priority: high
complexity: low
tags: [phase-1, backend, feature]
relevant_files:
  - internal/domain/ingredient.go
  - internal/domain/recipe.go
  - internal/domain/ingredient_test.go
  - internal/domain/recipe_test.go
must_not_touch:
  - cmd/
  - go.mod
depends_on: []
agent_skills: backend
created: 2026-08-24
---

## Context
The imerscafe backend must establish deterministic domain types for ingredients and recipes before implementing services, handlers, or AI integration. This spec introduces foundational `Ingredient` and `Recipe` types from the legacy Spring Boot implementation.

## Requirements
### Functional
- Define `Ingredient` type with English identifiers internally (IngredientCoffee, IngredientMilk, etc.) while preserving Portuguese API values (CAFE, LEITE, etc.)
- Support all 11 ingredients: Coffee, Milk, Chocolate, Foam, Whipped Cream, Caramel, Cinnamon, Sugar, Vanilla, Cream, Ice
- Define `Recipe` type with name, expected ingredient set, and base score
- Define 4 initial recipes:
  - Cappuccino: Coffee, Milk, Foam (score 10)
  - Mocha: Coffee, Chocolate, Milk (score 12)
  - Latte: Coffee, Milk, Vanilla (score 8)
  - Café com Chantilly: Coffee, Whipped Cream, Caramel (score 15)

### Non-Functional
- Types must serialize to JSON with Portuguese values
- Types must use English identifiers and naming
- No HTTP, AI, or persistence package dependencies
- Testable with deterministic, idempotent inputs

## Acceptance Criteria
### Automated
- [ ] Unit tests cover all 11 ingredients with English/Portuguese mappings
- [ ] Unit tests verify 4 recipes with exact ingredient sets and scores
- [ ] `go fmt ./internal/domain` produces no changes
- [ ] `go vet ./internal/domain` completes without warnings
- [ ] Tests pass with `go test ./internal/domain/...`

### Manual
- [ ] English identifiers used consistently
- [ ] Portuguese external values preserved in serialization
- [ ] Matches legacy Spring Boot implementation

## Constraints
- Do not import HTTP, database, or AI packages
- Do not use external frameworks
- Ingredient/recipe definitions must be deterministic constants or closed sets
```

